## [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#step-1-create-an-api-key)  Step 1: Create an API key

1. [Register for an account](https://api.together.ai/) if you don’t have one.
2. Go to your project’s [API keys page](https://api.together.ai/settings/projects/~current/api-keys).
3. Select **Create key**, give it a name, and copy the value. New keys are only shown once, so make sure to save it somewhere safe.
4. Set the key as an environment variable in your terminal:

macOS / Linux

Windows (PowerShell)

```
export TOGETHER_API_KEY="your_api_key"
```

```
$env:TOGETHER_API_KEY="your_api_key"
```

The SDK reads `TOGETHER_API_KEY` automatically when you call `Together()`. Pass `api_key=` to the constructor to override it.

## [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#step-2-install-the-sdk)  Step 2: Install the SDK

Together AI publishes official SDKs for Python and TypeScript. You can also use the [OpenAI SDK](https://docs.together.ai/docs/inference/openai-compatibility) pointed at the Together base URL, or call the [REST API](https://docs.together.ai/reference/chat-completions) directly from any language.

Python (uv)

Python (pip)

TypeScript (npm)

```
uv init --no-workspace # optional
uv add together
```

```
pip install together
```

```
npm install together-ai
```

## [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#step-3-run-your-first-query)  Step 3: Run your first query

The example below sends a chat completion request to [MiniMax M3.1 Flash](https://docs.together.ai/docs/serverless/models) and prints the response:

Python

TypeScript

cURL

```
from together import Together

client = Together()  # reads TOGETHER_API_KEY from environment

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {\
            "role": "user",\
            "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?",\
        }\
    ],
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
```

```
import Together from "together-ai";

const together = new Together(); // reads TOGETHER_API_KEY from environment

async function main() {
  const response = await together.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      { role: "user", content: "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?" },\
    ],
  });

  console.log(response.choices[0].message.content);
}

main();
```

```
curl -X POST "https://api.together.ai/v1/chat/completions" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOGETHER_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    "messages": [\
      {"role": "user", "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?"}\
    ]
  }'
```

Save the snippet to a file, then run it. (The cURL command runs directly in your terminal.)

Python (uv)

Python (pip)

TypeScript

```
uv run main.py
```

```
python main.py
```

```
npx tsx main.ts
```

After a few seconds, you should see the response printed to your terminal.

## [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#going-further)  Going further

Try some of these variations to see what else the model can do:

### [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#stream-the-response)  Stream the response

Streaming returns the response token by token as it’s generated, instead of making you wait for the full reply. This is especially helpful with a [reasoning model](https://docs.together.ai/docs/inference/chat/reasoning) like MiniMax M3.1 Flash, which works through a problem before answering and can produce a lot of output.A reasoning model’s response has two parts: the step-by-step thinking and the final answer. The thinking arrives in `reasoning_content` or `reasoning`, depending on the model, and the answer arrives in `content`.Set `stream=True` (Python) or `stream: true` (TypeScript/cURL) and read the thinking and the answer off each chunk’s `delta`:

Python

TypeScript

cURL

```
from together import Together

client = Together()  # reads TOGETHER_API_KEY from environment

stream = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {\
            "role": "user",\
            "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?",\
        }\
    ],
    stream=True,
)

printed_answer_header = False

for chunk in stream:
    if not chunk.choices:
        continue
    delta = chunk.choices[0].delta

    # Reasoning models return their thinking in `reasoning_content` or
    # `reasoning`, depending on the model.
    thinking = getattr(delta, "reasoning_content", None) or getattr(
        delta, "reasoning", None
    )
    if thinking:
        print(thinking, end="", flush=True)

    # The final answer arrives in `content`.
    if getattr(delta, "content", None):
        if not printed_answer_header:
            print("\n\n--- Answer ---\n", flush=True)
            printed_answer_header = True
        print(delta.content, end="", flush=True)
```

```
import Together from "together-ai";

const together = new Together();

async function main() {
  const stream = await together.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      { role: "user", content: "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?" },\
    ],
    stream: true,
  });

  let printedAnswerHeader = false;

  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    const delta = chunk.choices[0]?.delta;

    // Reasoning models return their thinking in `reasoning_content` or
    // `reasoning`, depending on the model.
    const thinking = delta?.reasoning_content || delta?.reasoning;
    if (thinking) process.stdout.write(thinking);

    // The final answer arrives in `content`.
    if (delta?.content) {
      if (!printedAnswerHeader) {
        process.stdout.write("\n\n--- Answer ---\n");
        printedAnswerHeader = true;
      }
      process.stdout.write(delta.content);
    }
  }
}

main();
```

```
curl -N -X POST "https://api.together.ai/v1/chat/completions" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOGETHER_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    "messages": [\
      {"role": "user", "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?"}\
    ],
    "stream": true
  }'
```

With a non-reasoning model, both reasoning fields stay empty and only `content` is returned, so the same loop works unchanged.

### [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#add-a-system-prompt)  Add a system prompt

Prepend a `system` message to set the model’s tone, role, or constraints:

Python

TypeScript

```
from together import Together

client = Together()

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {\
            "role": "system",\
            "content": "You are a concise travel guide. Answer in two sentences or fewer.",\
        },\
        {\
            "role": "user",\
            "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?",\
        },\
    ],
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
```

```
import Together from "together-ai";

const together = new Together();

async function main() {
  const response = await together.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      {\
        role: "system",\
        content:\
          "You are a concise travel guide. Answer in two sentences or fewer.",\
      },\
      { role: "user", content: "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?" },\
    ],
  });

  console.log(response.choices[0].message.content);
}

main();
```

### [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#get-structured-json-output)  Get structured JSON output

Pass a [JSON schema](https://docs.together.ai/docs/inference/chat/structured-outputs) via `response_format` to get parseable JSON back:

Python

TypeScript

```
from pydantic import BaseModel
from together import Together

client = Together()

class Activity(BaseModel):
    name: str
    neighborhood: str
    why: str

class Itinerary(BaseModel):
    city: str
    activities: list[Activity]

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {"role": "user", "content": "Suggest 3 things to do in New York."},\
    ],
    response_format={
        "type": "json_schema",
        "json_schema": {
            "name": "Itinerary",
            "schema": Itinerary.model_json_schema(),
        },
    },
)

itinerary = Itinerary.model_validate_json(response.choices[0].message.content)
print(itinerary)
```

```
import Together from "together-ai";
import { z } from "zod";

const together = new Together();

const Itinerary = z.object({
  city: z.string(),
  activities: z.array(
    z.object({
      name: z.string(),
      neighborhood: z.string(),
      why: z.string(),
    }),
  ),
});

async function main() {
  const response = await together.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      { role: "user", content: "Suggest 3 things to do in New York." },\
    ],
    response_format: {
      type: "json_schema",
      json_schema: { name: "Itinerary", schema: z.toJSONSchema(Itinerary) },
    },
  });

  const itinerary = Itinerary.parse(
    JSON.parse(response.choices[0].message.content!),
  );
  console.log(itinerary);
}

main();
```

### [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#analyze-an-image)  Analyze an image

MiniMax M3.1 Flash also accepts images. Add an `image_url` block to the user message to ask questions about a picture:

Python

TypeScript

```
from together import Together

client = Together()

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {\
            "role": "user",\
            "content": [\
                {\
                    "type": "text",\
                    "text": "Describe this image in one sentence.",\
                },\
                {\
                    "type": "image_url",\
                    "image_url": {\
                        "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/patrickvonplaten/random_img/resolve/main/yosemite.png"\
                    },\
                },\
            ],\
        }\
    ],
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
```

```
import Together from "together-ai";

const together = new Together();

async function main() {
  const response = await together.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      {\
        role: "user",\
        content: [\
          { type: "text", text: "Describe this image in one sentence." },\
          {\
            type: "image_url",\
            image_url: {\
              url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/patrickvonplaten/random_img/resolve/main/yosemite.png",\
            },\
          },\
        ],\
      },\
    ],
  });

  console.log(response.choices[0].message.content);
}

main();
```

### [​](https://docs.together.ai/docs/quickstart\#use-the-openai-sdk)  Use the OpenAI SDK

If you’re already using the OpenAI SDK, you can point it at Together’s base URL (`https://api.together.ai/v1`) and keep the rest of your code the same:

Python

TypeScript

```
import os
from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(
    api_key=os.environ["TOGETHER_API_KEY"],
    base_url="https://api.together.ai/v1",
)

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages=[\
        {\
            "role": "user",\
            "content": "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?",\
        }\
    ],
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
```

```
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: process.env.TOGETHER_API_KEY,
  baseURL: "https://api.together.ai/v1",
});

async function main() {
  const response = await client.chat.completions.create({
    model: "MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash",
    messages: [\
      { role: "user", content: "What are the top 3 things to do in New York?" },\
    ],
  });

  console.log(response.choices[0].message.content);
}

main();
```

See [OpenAI compatibility](https://docs.together.ai/docs/inference/openai-compatibility) for the full list of supported endpoints and parameters.

